1
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:11,460
I'm sorry...

2
00:00:12,530 --> 00:00:13,420
I'm sorry...

3
00:00:15,470 --> 00:00:18,110
Why are you crying?

4
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:22,190
Because I left you alone...

5
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:25,500
You did?

6
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,950
Because I couldn't find 
you for all this time...

7
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:36,230
But... I'm right here.

8
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:42,270
What's your name?

9
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:47,910
My name is...

10
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:10,880
I know this is just a dream world,

11
00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:14,770
but I can smell the wind 
and even feel the dirt.

12
00:01:14,770 --> 00:01:16,710
It's so strange, isn't it?

13
00:01:17,570 --> 00:01:20,100
Echidna? Are you listening?

14
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:26,600
I'm sorry! Are you all right?

15
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:28,890
Was I walking too quickly?

16
00:01:28,890 --> 00:01:30,660
Did you think such transparent sympathy

17
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:33,360
would change my attitude in the least?

18
00:01:33,730 --> 00:01:35,240
You're quite foolish, if so.

19
00:01:36,190 --> 00:01:38,860
Oh, please. I was just worried about you.

20
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:41,680
I need none of your concern whatsoever.

21
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:45,180
There were a few too many dreams 
happening at once, that's all.

22
00:01:45,180 --> 00:01:46,910
It will adjust itself soon.

23
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:48,430
Just like this.

24
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:49,670
See?

25
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:54,630
"Dream world" is merely 
a figurative expression.

26
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:58,620
More accurately, it's a separate 
world that replicates the memories

27
00:01:58,620 --> 00:02:02,100
and reflects the consciousness 
of those who undergo the trial.

28
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:06,870
Thank you for explaining it so clearly,
 even though you hate me.

29
00:02:06,870 --> 00:02:11,990
Just don't go getting any silly ideas 
about me actually being a very nice person.

30
00:02:11,990 --> 00:02:15,640
It's simply my nature to answer 
any questions asked of me.

31
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:17,020
Yes, of course.

32
00:02:19,770 --> 00:02:24,090
Do you remember the pathetic struggle you 
endured the last time you attempted the trial?

33
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:29,170
I was so helpless, I can't even argue 
with that mean description of it.

34
00:02:29,570 --> 00:02:33,410
I must have covered up my memories 
because I didn't want to see them.

35
00:02:33,410 --> 00:02:37,140
That's why I can't recall them on my own.

36
00:02:37,990 --> 00:02:39,180
And even now,

37
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:43,100
I'm still not prepared.

38
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:46,740
So it would be no surprise 
if you failed again?

39
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:50,000
Creating a line of defense before you 
even start is awfully defeatist.

40
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:52,310
No, it's not that.

41
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:56,310
I'm going to prepare myself right now.

42
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:03,120
This is no ordinary tree, is it?

43
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:06,910
There was something you desperately 
wanted to keep locked up inside it.

44
00:03:06,910 --> 00:03:08,500
This is the Princess Room.

45
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:12,480
I was sent to play here 
often when I was little.

46
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:15,090
Oh, right... I can't touch the door.

47
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:17,370
Can we just walk through it?

48
00:03:39,410 --> 00:03:41,480
That young one is you, right?

49
00:03:41,970 --> 00:03:43,780
Even considering you knew nothing yet,

50
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:46,610
you look so irritatingly carefree.

51
00:03:46,610 --> 00:03:49,050
Must you even complain 
about my younger self?

52
00:03:49,810 --> 00:03:51,700
Besides, now I...

53
00:04:01,630 --> 00:04:03,240
Mother Fortuna...

54
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:07,800
Emilia, I need to go take 
care of something important.

55
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:10,380
So stay in this room and be good, all right?

56
00:04:10,770 --> 00:04:12,910
"Something important" again?

57
00:04:15,730 --> 00:04:18,320
You have my brother's silver hair...

58
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:22,500
But your kind features 
come from your mother.

59
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:24,450
Everyone in my family has mean eyes.

60
00:04:25,310 --> 00:04:28,160
I like your eyes, Mother Fortuna!

61
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:31,900
Mother Fortuna was my 
father's younger sister.

62
00:04:32,310 --> 00:04:36,170
My real parents were too 
busy to spend time with me,

63
00:04:36,750 --> 00:04:39,820
so I was left in Mother Fortuna's care.

64
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:51,430
I'm so bored!

65
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:55,980
And Mother always tells me lying 
and keeping secrets are wrong!

66
00:04:55,980 --> 00:04:57,120
Right?!

67
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:00,400
I wish I could go outside.

68
00:05:06,950 --> 00:05:08,300
A fairy?

69
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,700
Hey, no fair! Wait!

70
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:33,680
Mother Fortuna and everyone 
else keeps secrets from me,

71
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:34,810
so we're even!

72
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:43,370
Sneaky, sneak...

73
00:05:46,150 --> 00:05:46,990
Sneak...

74
00:05:57,590 --> 00:06:01,630
You've all done so much for us.

75
00:06:01,630 --> 00:06:06,230
And we have put you through so much trouble.

76
00:06:06,230 --> 00:06:08,430
Well, that goes for both of us,

77
00:06:08,430 --> 00:06:09,290
Geuse.

78
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:12,260
Also...

79
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:14,920
I know I ask this every time we meet,

80
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:17,730
but is the seal intact?

81
00:06:18,110 --> 00:06:20,360
Don't worry. Nothing has changed.

82
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,480
If the worst were to happen,

83
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:25,520
I could never face my brother and sister.

84
00:06:26,070 --> 00:06:28,450
You mean your brother... and his wife?

85
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:31,090
It's all right. I know.

86
00:06:31,570 --> 00:06:36,920
But I must never forget the weight 
of the responsibility I carry.

87
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:39,770
I don't want to abandon it or 
see it only partway through.

88
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:41,670
Isn't the same true for you?

89
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:43,150
I...

90
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:47,420
I have nothing else, after all.

91
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:51,840
I suppose it's a different sense 
of responsibility from yours.

92
00:06:52,430 --> 00:06:54,150
Obsession, regret...

93
00:06:54,930 --> 00:06:57,810
I'm only clinging to things that 
might as well be delusions.

94
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:03,250
Thanks to the spirits,

95
00:07:03,250 --> 00:07:06,280
the seasons don't change much in the forest,

96
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:08,900
but you continue to bring us 
things like clothing and books.

97
00:07:09,450 --> 00:07:10,860
We truly appreciate it.

98
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:13,870
Thank you, as always.

99
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:17,890
In truth, it is wrong to force all of you

100
00:07:17,890 --> 00:07:21,870
to live in such inconvenience 
in a place like this.

101
00:07:22,450 --> 00:07:24,910
Don't call it "a place like this."

102
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:27,670
We love the forest, you know.

103
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:29,470
Fortuna-sama!

104
00:07:30,610 --> 00:07:32,690
All of the items have been transferred.

105
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:34,750
Thank you, Archi.

106
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:38,350
You've grown even more dependable 
as well, Archi-dono.

107
00:07:38,590 --> 00:07:41,230
As part of the next generation 
of forest dwellers,

108
00:07:41,230 --> 00:07:43,600
I cannot be regarded as a novice forever.

109
00:07:44,410 --> 00:07:46,360
I pray your good health will persist.

110
00:07:46,790 --> 00:07:48,340
For the forest and the seal,

111
00:07:49,030 --> 00:07:51,260
for your family, and for yourself, too.

112
00:07:58,320 --> 00:08:01,120
Oh, yes... Just one last thing.

113
00:08:01,890 --> 00:08:04,250
Is Emilia-sama in good health?

114
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:07,390
Don't worry.

115
00:08:07,390 --> 00:08:10,880
Emilia is growing into a very good,
 very healthy girl.

116
00:08:11,410 --> 00:08:12,620
But... I'm sorry.

117
00:08:13,020 --> 00:08:14,680
I can't let her meet you.

118
00:08:15,050 --> 00:08:16,160
It's all right.

119
00:08:16,520 --> 00:08:20,670
As long as Emilia-sama grows 
up healthy, that's enough.

120
00:08:21,090 --> 00:08:25,740
A sinner such as myself could 
never dare to ask for more.

121
00:08:28,230 --> 00:08:31,180
Bishop Romanée-Conti, are you ready?

122
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:32,780
Yes, I'm finished.

123
00:08:33,190 --> 00:08:35,970
Let us sinners be on our way.

124
00:08:36,690 --> 00:08:39,620
May we meet again soon, Fortuna-sama.

125
00:08:40,420 --> 00:08:42,560
Even if no one else will say it,

126
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:44,930
we are grateful to you.

127
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:47,080
I really mean that.

128
00:08:47,510 --> 00:08:53,500
Your words alone would surely carry me 
through a hundred years of turmoil.

129
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:07,600
Fortuna-sama, are you tired?

130
00:09:08,030 --> 00:09:10,790
Don't treat me like such an old lady.

131
00:09:11,150 --> 00:09:14,530
I know I'm old compared 
to a young boy like you,

132
00:09:14,530 --> 00:09:15,820
but I'm still in very good shape!

133
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:18,720
Th-That wasn't what I meant at all!

134
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:22,520
I just thought this must be hard, when you
 also have the duty of the forest dwellers...

135
00:09:23,090 --> 00:09:25,790
Then perhaps I'll take advantage 
of your kindness...

136
00:09:26,370 --> 00:09:28,100
And let you handle the rest.

137
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:33,220
I need to go and free a little 
princess who must be very bored.

138
00:09:35,760 --> 00:09:38,080
What do I do? What do I do? 
What do I do? What do I do?

139
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:39,450
What do I do? What do—

140
00:09:40,410 --> 00:09:41,930
What do I do? What do I do? What—

141
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,520
What do I do? What do I do?

142
00:09:45,010 --> 00:09:47,060
What do I do? What do I do? What do I do?

143
00:09:54,230 --> 00:09:55,650
Wow...

144
00:09:56,020 --> 00:09:57,810
Emilia, are you awake?

145
00:09:57,810 --> 00:09:58,810
Eep!

146
00:09:58,810 --> 00:10:00,480
I-I'm awake!

147
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:02,300
B-But...

148
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:03,440
What?

149
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:05,250
Why are you so flustered?

150
00:10:08,190 --> 00:10:11,290
Um... I-I'm sorry.

151
00:10:11,290 --> 00:10:14,370
I spilled a bunch of my drawing ink.

152
00:10:14,910 --> 00:10:16,410
Oh, dear...

153
00:10:16,410 --> 00:10:19,120
Mother Fortuna, I...

154
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:21,930
Honestly, you worry too much, Emilia.

155
00:10:22,510 --> 00:10:25,820
You don't need to be so afraid.
 I'm not angry.

156
00:10:26,660 --> 00:10:28,640
But you're not hurt, are you?

157
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:34,150
Mother?

158
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:37,040
Oh, it's nothing.

159
00:10:37,730 --> 00:10:41,150
I just missed you so, so much.

160
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:45,520
Spoiled child...

161
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:48,690
Hey, Emilia...

162
00:10:50,820 --> 00:10:52,080
I love you.

163
00:10:55,730 --> 00:10:59,730
Perhaps the sights you had locked 
deep within your heart have begun

164
00:10:59,730 --> 00:11:02,260
to overlap with scenes from your 
memories, little by little?

165
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:03,650
I'm surprised.

166
00:11:03,650 --> 00:11:08,270
I thought you'd have some stinging 
comments to make about Mother and me.

167
00:11:08,850 --> 00:11:10,730
Even if that's what you thought,

168
00:11:10,730 --> 00:11:13,660
I wouldn't recommend coming 
out and saying so.

169
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:16,990
My opinion of you is already low enough,

170
00:11:16,990 --> 00:11:19,730
and you're making it plummet further.

171
00:11:19,730 --> 00:11:21,370
Oh, don't worry.

172
00:11:21,370 --> 00:11:24,200
I won't tell anyone else about this.

173
00:11:25,570 --> 00:11:27,380
For better or for worse,

174
00:11:27,380 --> 00:11:30,830
his influence on you has 
grown increasingly strong.

175
00:11:31,170 --> 00:11:32,120
Really?

176
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:34,000
Thanks!

177
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:37,790
Anyway, now you've recalled

178
00:11:37,790 --> 00:11:42,340
your mother, some people you knew,
 and that so-called fairy...

179
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:44,380
Are you ready to face your past now?

180
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:46,510
No, not yet.

181
00:11:48,450 --> 00:11:51,740
There are still important 
memories I'm missing.

182
00:11:52,410 --> 00:11:53,730
What more could there be?

183
00:11:56,210 --> 00:11:57,180
The seal.

184
00:12:00,580 --> 00:12:04,820
Come on, little fairy. 
We're escaping again today.

185
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:07,940
Emilia, I'm coming in.

186
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:08,700
Eep!

187
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:12,290
What's the matter?

188
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:15,980
Wh-What about you, Archi? 
What was it you needed?

189
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:19,120
Well, first, I brought some snacks for you.

190
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:19,800
They're nuts.

191
00:12:20,970 --> 00:12:23,340
Eat these and be a good girl, all right?

192
00:12:25,090 --> 00:12:26,350
Thank you...

193
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:30,430
Archi has been a real worrywart lately.

194
00:12:30,430 --> 00:12:31,770
I need to be careful.

195
00:12:33,090 --> 00:12:33,810
Sneaky, sneak...

196
00:12:34,410 --> 00:12:36,770
Geuse's group is here again today.

197
00:12:37,490 --> 00:12:40,670
I thought whatever they were 
hiding would be more fun.

198
00:12:40,670 --> 00:12:42,610
Mother and the rest are so weird.

199
00:12:43,470 --> 00:12:46,800
Emilia has been so full of energy lately.

200
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:49,530
She always comes home with 
her clothes all muddy.

201
00:12:49,530 --> 00:12:52,620
That she is so healthy can 
only be a good thing.

202
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:54,710
I'll bring as many new 
clothes for her as I can.

203
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:57,060
I'm sorry if I seem to be demanding more

204
00:12:57,060 --> 00:12:59,190
when you've already done so much.

205
00:12:59,970 --> 00:13:01,540
Do you have adult clothes, too?

206
00:13:01,930 --> 00:13:03,090
Yes, of course.

207
00:13:03,710 --> 00:13:07,840
I'm sure we have something 
that will look lovely on you.

208
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:11,950
Hey, I know we've known 
each other a long time,

209
00:13:11,950 --> 00:13:14,100
but when did you start 
making jokes like that?

210
00:13:15,350 --> 00:13:17,810
I only told what I feel to be the truth...

211
00:13:17,810 --> 00:13:20,320
Was there something strange 
about what I said?

212
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:30,350
Geuse, what is this?

213
00:13:30,350 --> 00:13:33,020
Oh, I just remembered another time

214
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:36,150
when you seemed unhappy while talking to me,

215
00:13:36,150 --> 00:13:38,860
and it was because you had a fever.

216
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:41,210
You don't feel warm right now...

217
00:13:41,210 --> 00:13:44,290
Come on, that was decades ago!

218
00:13:44,290 --> 00:13:46,080
Don't treat me like a child!

219
00:13:46,530 --> 00:13:47,930
Honestly...

220
00:13:50,130 --> 00:13:51,660
Stupid Geuse!

221
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:53,640
And stupid Archi, too!

222
00:13:56,740 --> 00:14:00,190
So... is the seal still in place?

223
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:02,240
As always, yes.

224
00:14:03,180 --> 00:14:06,540
It's very conscientious of you 
to check on it every time.

225
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:08,420
That is my duty, after all.

226
00:14:09,030 --> 00:14:11,950
The state of affairs outside the 
forest is dubious at the moment.

227
00:14:12,570 --> 00:14:14,350
Perhaps my concern is baseless,

228
00:14:14,350 --> 00:14:16,250
but I wanted you to be aware.

229
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:17,910
I understand.

230
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:20,140
Please remain diligent.

231
00:14:20,650 --> 00:14:24,130
For Emilia-sama, and for 
the two of them, too.

232
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:26,130
Seal?

233
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:33,060
Yes, please!

234
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:54,650
A door?

235
00:14:55,670 --> 00:14:57,430
What a strange sight.

236
00:15:01,170 --> 00:15:03,240
This is... the seal.

237
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:12,340
This seal's existence... is why...

238
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:16,970
You found the answer?

239
00:15:27,210 --> 00:15:29,200
This is the seal?

240
00:15:34,880 --> 00:15:40,000
Some other guy saw my love letter 
to the girl I like before she did.

241
00:15:40,260 --> 00:15:42,060
My life is over.

242
00:15:42,060 --> 00:15:45,040
You're way too damn depressed about this!

243
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:47,280
C'mon, get it together, man!

244
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:51,810
I never imagined Garfiel would be there,
waiting to settle the score...

245
00:15:51,810 --> 00:15:55,010
You're always hitting on her 
in front of people, anyway.

246
00:15:55,010 --> 00:15:58,480
Why get so embarrassed just because 
you put it in writing this time?

247
00:15:58,480 --> 00:16:01,390
I'm prepared for her to just 
brush it off any other time!

248
00:16:01,390 --> 00:16:04,320
And that's exactly what always 
happens, so it's fine then!

249
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:06,880
But I was being serious this time!

250
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:10,020
And it was literally a 
late-night love letter.

251
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:11,790
The most embarrassing kind!

252
00:16:11,790 --> 00:16:14,000
Don't worry, boss.

253
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:17,750
If anything, it made me wish 
I could sponge off of your luck.

254
00:16:17,750 --> 00:16:20,750
"In matters of love, follow the 
lingdorn's example," as they say.

255
00:16:20,750 --> 00:16:22,950
When <i>you</i> say that,

256
00:16:22,950 --> 00:16:26,000
it sounds like you're instigating, 
even if you're not!

257
00:16:27,170 --> 00:16:30,700
It took Garfiel about an 
hour when he went in,

258
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:32,380
so I guess it'll take her about that long.

259
00:16:32,620 --> 00:16:34,980
If she's successful, yes.

260
00:16:35,470 --> 00:16:36,350
Ow!

261
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:39,090
Try to take a hint for a change.

262
00:16:39,850 --> 00:16:40,960
Ouch!

263
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:42,660
You're that oblivious to the mood,

264
00:16:42,660 --> 00:16:43,970
and you call yourself a merchant?

265
00:16:43,970 --> 00:16:46,900
That hurt even more than the forehead flick!

266
00:16:46,060 --> 00:16:46,900
Anyway...

267
00:16:47,770 --> 00:16:50,630
Shima-sama wants to talk to you, Barusu.

268
00:16:50,630 --> 00:16:53,030
She wants to continue 
last night's discussion.

269
00:16:53,470 --> 00:16:57,220
What did you and Gran— 
the old hag talk about?

270
00:16:57,220 --> 00:16:58,500
There's no point in saying it over.

271
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:01,330
We all know you're a Granny's boy.

272
00:17:01,330 --> 00:17:04,370
Mostly, she told me what happened 
when you went into the graveyard.

273
00:17:05,150 --> 00:17:06,580
Oh, really?

274
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:10,690
I had my hands full yesterday figuring 
out how to deal with Garfiel.

275
00:17:10,690 --> 00:17:13,600
We ended up putting off 
the important part.

276
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:15,740
Just what did you put off?

277
00:17:16,420 --> 00:17:17,390
Well...

278
00:17:17,390 --> 00:17:23,020
A subject that is unavoidable if you 
wish to liberate the Sanctuary.

279
00:17:31,090 --> 00:17:33,390
Hngh... Hngh... Hngh...

280
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:37,530
Why won't it just fall over?

281
00:17:38,030 --> 00:17:40,360
It's a little too weird 
for me to understand.

282
00:17:40,790 --> 00:17:43,820
But thanks to all of you, 
I managed to find it!

283
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:46,000
Clap, clap, clap!

284
00:17:47,150 --> 00:17:50,770
Hmph. It's all Mother Fortuna's fault.

285
00:17:50,770 --> 00:17:52,470
And Geuse's fault.

286
00:17:53,060 --> 00:17:54,460
Nyah!

287
00:17:57,140 --> 00:18:00,020
All right, time to go home.

288
00:18:00,020 --> 00:18:04,520
Today, the painter feels like coloring 
the sky red and the forest white!

289
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:10,380
What's wrong?

290
00:18:15,940 --> 00:18:18,370
Could it be... something's about to happen?

291
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:26,540
This is quite a problem.

292
00:18:27,810 --> 00:18:30,240
I might not make it by the appointed time.

293
00:18:32,600 --> 00:18:36,190
Oh? And whose cute little 
behind might that be?

294
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:42,550
I implore you to grant me temperate mercy...

295
00:18:42,550 --> 00:18:46,980
Well, well! What an adorable young lady—

296
00:18:49,890 --> 00:18:51,860
A-Are you...

297
00:18:52,230 --> 00:18:55,360
No, you couldn't be...

298
00:18:57,220 --> 00:18:58,070
Geuse?

299
00:18:59,630 --> 00:19:00,570
Are you all right?

300
00:19:10,450 --> 00:19:12,080
I am... fine...

301
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:16,900
Yes... Yes! Of course I'm all right!

302
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:18,840
Nothing is wrong in the slightest!

303
00:19:19,540 --> 00:19:20,840
Because I...

304
00:19:21,770 --> 00:19:25,120
I... I have just...

305
00:19:26,530 --> 00:19:30,930
been granted salvation like never before!

306
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:34,750
Really?

307
00:19:35,930 --> 00:19:38,230
You got saved, but you're crying?

308
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:42,100
I'm not crying because I'm sad.

309
00:19:42,550 --> 00:19:45,810
I'm so happy... I'm so overjoyed.

310
00:19:46,210 --> 00:19:47,790
I'm so truly blessed...

311
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:52,210
And such happiness can bring 
warm tears sometimes.

312
00:20:01,130 --> 00:20:04,430
You cry... even when you're happy?

313
00:20:06,590 --> 00:20:09,040
It's all right, Geuse.

314
00:20:09,570 --> 00:20:10,680
It's all right.

315
00:20:12,390 --> 00:20:13,630
It's all right.

316
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:22,100
I know there are so many things 
like this that I'd forgotten...

317
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:26,820
But not too long ago, I wouldn't 
have been able to accept this.

318
00:20:27,620 --> 00:20:28,760
Still, right now...

319
00:20:30,850 --> 00:20:33,750
I'm scared, but I won't cower in fear.

320
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:37,240
You're giving up on the decision to 
depend on a man or father figure,

321
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:41,090
even though it's so typical 
of a filthy woman like you?

322
00:20:41,090 --> 00:20:44,590
I'm sure Subaru would 
forgive me if I did that,

323
00:20:45,210 --> 00:20:47,230
but I'd still be weak,

324
00:20:47,230 --> 00:20:48,990
and I don't want to just shrug off that fact.

325
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:50,560
Besides...

326
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:55,690
I don't want all those things Subaru 
wrote for me to end up being wrong.

327
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:58,420
Subaru believes in me,

328
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:01,560
and that's why I don't want to 
be embarrassed by his feelings.

329
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:04,650
Do as you wish.

330
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:09,260
I will simply find satisfaction 
in your suffering.

331
00:21:11,470 --> 00:21:13,580
So everything is ready now?

332
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:17,050
Yes. The warm-up round is over.

333
00:21:17,530 --> 00:21:21,500
The trial that broke you 
once now begins for real.

334
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:24,930
Please wait, Emilia-sama!

335
00:21:24,930 --> 00:21:26,970
It's dangerous to run around like that!

336
00:21:26,970 --> 00:21:28,570
Nope! Nope!

337
00:21:28,570 --> 00:21:30,760
Come on! Just try to catch me!

338
00:21:32,880 --> 00:21:36,860
Her mischief is too much 
for us to handle, too.

339
00:21:37,450 --> 00:21:39,670
To have so much energy is a good thing.

340
00:21:39,670 --> 00:21:43,400
I just... wish she would avoid 
doing anything dangerous.

341
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:46,270
If she could just jump around in her home,

342
00:21:46,270 --> 00:21:48,310
healthy and bathed in sunlight,

343
00:21:48,310 --> 00:21:50,880
with no concerns about breaking anything...

344
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:52,240
Geuse...

345
00:21:52,530 --> 00:21:54,950
That would be very difficult.

346
00:21:56,770 --> 00:21:58,190
W-Would it?

347
00:21:58,690 --> 00:22:01,890
But for Emilia-sama's sake, I just...

348
00:22:01,890 --> 00:22:03,090
I just...

349
00:22:04,630 --> 00:22:05,420
Hey!

350
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:09,880
Mother and Geuse! Why aren't 
either of you chasing me?

351
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:12,510
Aren't we playing chase right now?!

352
00:22:12,900 --> 00:22:15,120
Ah, please forgive me!

353
00:22:15,120 --> 00:22:17,610
Never have I made such a terrible mistake!

354
00:22:18,020 --> 00:22:19,980
Don't spoil her like that.

355
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:22,480
Emilia, come here.

356
00:22:23,030 --> 00:22:24,690
What is it, Mother?

357
00:22:25,210 --> 00:22:28,070
Honestly, you're so spoiled.

358
00:22:28,500 --> 00:22:29,550
Eep!

359
00:22:29,550 --> 00:22:30,880
Too bad!

360
00:22:30,880 --> 00:22:34,210
You've been captured by Mother Fortuna!

361
00:22:34,210 --> 00:22:36,240
No fair! That's cheating, Mother!

362
00:22:36,240 --> 00:22:38,390
That's wrong! That's dirty! Say you're sorry!

363
00:22:38,390 --> 00:22:41,370
Goodness, just listen to this girl!

364
00:22:41,370 --> 00:22:45,920
Are you thinking about 
what I said to you, then?

365
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:49,130
Why do you think Geuse 
and I were chasing you?

366
00:22:50,360 --> 00:22:52,600
N-No, Mother!

367
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:56,890
The fairies said we should 
go outside and play, so I...

368
00:22:57,280 --> 00:23:02,320
I don't like children who blame things 
on other people—rather, fairies.

369
00:23:04,400 --> 00:23:05,810
I'm sorry.

370
00:23:05,810 --> 00:23:08,350
Since I made friends with Geuse,

371
00:23:08,350 --> 00:23:11,160
I wanted to tell you about it.

372
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:13,380
And since Geuse is a crybaby,

373
00:23:13,380 --> 00:23:14,910
I felt like I had to help him.

374
00:23:15,300 --> 00:23:17,970
That feeling is very precious.

375
00:23:17,970 --> 00:23:22,320
But we made a promise that you'd 
never go to that place, didn't we?

376
00:23:23,040 --> 00:23:25,130
Y-Yes... we did.

377
00:23:25,570 --> 00:23:28,390
That was a very bad thing to do.

378
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:34,890
A promise is the embodiment of trust,

379
00:23:35,390 --> 00:23:40,510
and to break it is to betray that trust,
 so you mustn't do it.

380
00:23:41,190 --> 00:23:44,170
Promise me, Emilia,

381
00:23:44,170 --> 00:23:47,200
that you'll keep your promises from now on.

382
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:50,780
Yes... I will.

383
00:23:51,240 --> 00:23:53,960
I'm sorry, Mother...

384
00:23:55,540 --> 00:23:56,280
All right.

385
00:23:57,960 --> 00:23:59,230
That's good enough.

386
00:24:04,770 --> 00:24:07,680
And... what about you, 
Geuse? Are you all right?

387
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:12,360
I-It was just such a dazzling sight...

388
00:24:12,360 --> 00:24:15,420
I couldn't... I couldn't 
hold back my tears...

389
00:24:17,440 --> 00:24:19,240
Anyway, Emilia...

390
00:24:19,970 --> 00:24:22,250
You mentioned fairies?

391
00:24:22,250 --> 00:24:24,740
Oh, yeah! Fairies!

392
00:24:24,740 --> 00:24:27,490
They've been coming to 
help me for a long time!

393
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:28,860
Come on.

394
00:24:32,280 --> 00:24:34,120
Are these... lesser spirits?!

395
00:24:34,610 --> 00:24:36,640
And so many of them!

396
00:24:41,090 --> 00:24:46,250
It would seem that Emilia-sama possesses 
the natural talent to be a spirit user.

397
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:50,090
Lesser spirits? Natural talent 
to be... a spirit user?

398
00:24:50,420 --> 00:24:54,870
The things you call "fairies" are 
beings called lesser spirits.

399
00:24:55,280 --> 00:24:58,290
Those who communicate with them, 
form contracts with them,

400
00:24:58,290 --> 00:25:00,970
and borrow their powers are 
known as spirit users.

401
00:25:01,520 --> 00:25:03,560
And I can be one of those?

402
00:25:03,920 --> 00:25:07,140
Hey, don't give her any weird ideas.

403
00:25:07,140 --> 00:25:10,640
Emilia-sama will not 
remain so young forever.

404
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:15,450
When no one is by her side, 
in particular, they will be her strength.

405
00:25:15,780 --> 00:25:20,430
But that could be dangerous, 
and I can't let my sweet Emilia...

406
00:25:21,290 --> 00:25:23,860
I'm on Geuse's side today!

407
00:25:23,860 --> 00:25:26,920
I'm gonna be a spirit user! So there!

408
00:25:27,310 --> 00:25:29,780
See? She's taken you seriously.

409
00:25:29,780 --> 00:25:31,130
How will you take responsibility for this?

410
00:25:31,330 --> 00:25:34,090
Well... I don't know what to...

411
00:25:34,440 --> 00:25:35,200
Um...

412
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:37,470
What a dilemma.

413
00:25:40,130 --> 00:25:43,250
You know, Mother Fortuna and Geuse,

414
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:45,090
you're acting like a mommy and daddy.

415
00:25:45,090 --> 00:25:45,980
Wha—

416
00:25:47,300 --> 00:25:49,700
D-Don't say silly things like that!

417
00:25:49,700 --> 00:25:53,300
Geuse and I have known each other 
for a long time! That's why—

418
00:25:51,540 --> 00:25:53,300
That's right, Emilia-sama!

419
00:25:53,300 --> 00:25:55,140
To one with a lifespan as long as mine,

420
00:25:55,140 --> 00:25:57,640
even Fortuna-sama is basically a child.

421
00:25:58,180 --> 00:26:00,830
Now, calling me child 
is going a bit too far!

422
00:26:00,830 --> 00:26:03,500
Do you even know how old I am?!

423
00:26:03,500 --> 00:26:06,450
N-No, I didn't phrase that properly!

424
00:26:06,450 --> 00:26:09,490
Of course, I'm quite aware 
of your precise age,

425
00:26:09,490 --> 00:26:14,130
and you are certainly too beautiful 
and mature to be a child.

426
00:26:15,600 --> 00:26:16,740
Indeed, indeed.

427
00:26:17,280 --> 00:26:19,800
Very well, then. I'll forgive you.

428
00:26:21,120 --> 00:26:23,760
But you'd better be very, very sorry.

429
00:26:24,440 --> 00:26:25,230
Right...

430
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:31,550
At any rate, I've known Fortuna-sama 
for a long, long time.

431
00:26:31,940 --> 00:26:36,280
In fact, since the days when your 
mother and father were well—

432
00:26:36,280 --> 00:26:37,250
Geuse!

433
00:26:38,010 --> 00:26:39,940
F-Forgive me.

434
00:26:40,860 --> 00:26:42,990
My mother and father?

435
00:26:47,480 --> 00:26:49,320
I'm sorry, Emilia.

436
00:26:50,530 --> 00:26:52,740
We'll talk about that another time.

437
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:55,040
Go on back to your room.

438
00:26:55,930 --> 00:26:57,800
Another time?

439
00:26:58,680 --> 00:27:00,570
You'll really tell me, then?

440
00:27:03,250 --> 00:27:05,680
Be a good girl. I know you can do that.

441
00:27:06,360 --> 00:27:10,040
I'll let you see Geuse again soon, too.

442
00:27:10,040 --> 00:27:11,230
You really, really mean it?

443
00:27:11,570 --> 00:27:14,520
You promise? And you won't break it?

444
00:27:22,580 --> 00:27:24,660
Yes. I promise.

445
00:27:26,100 --> 00:27:30,700
It'll be a very, very important 
promise between you and me.

446
00:27:33,530 --> 00:27:34,660
All right, then.

447
00:27:35,190 --> 00:27:37,760
I'll go back to my room now.

448
00:27:43,220 --> 00:27:44,640
See you soon, Geuse.

449
00:27:45,060 --> 00:27:47,270
Try not to cry too much.

450
00:27:47,780 --> 00:27:49,890
That's a promise until we meet again.

451
00:27:51,590 --> 00:27:55,480
Of course. We will meet again soon.

452
00:28:05,120 --> 00:28:06,450
Someone's coming.

453
00:28:19,570 --> 00:28:20,230
Who are you?

454
00:28:28,800 --> 00:28:31,390
When you want to know someone's name,

455
00:28:31,590 --> 00:28:35,350
isn't it common courtesy 
to give your own first?

456
00:28:35,730 --> 00:28:38,680
This is the first time we've 
ever seen each other.

457
00:28:38,680 --> 00:28:43,300
We should be on equal footing as far 
as building a relationship goes,

458
00:28:43,300 --> 00:28:47,470
so why do you get to demand my name 
like you're so much better than me?

459
00:28:47,470 --> 00:28:51,040
For a man, you sure seem 
to like talking a lot.

460
00:28:50,480 --> 00:28:52,640
"For a man"?

461
00:28:52,640 --> 00:28:56,420
Thanks for showing me that you don't 
even know any men to compare me to.

462
00:28:56,740 --> 00:28:59,670
I can't just let that 
attitude slide, you know.

463
00:29:00,120 --> 00:29:03,630
You're disrespecting my individuality,
 my authority—

464
00:29:03,630 --> 00:29:04,670
That's enough!

465
00:29:04,670 --> 00:29:07,140
Stop talking as if you're drunk on yourself!

466
00:29:07,140 --> 00:29:08,640
Who are you?!

467
00:29:20,560 --> 00:29:23,980
Archbishop of the Witch's Cult,
representing Greed...

468
00:29:24,500 --> 00:29:26,510
Regulus Corneas.

469
00:29:26,950 --> 00:29:29,950
A Journey Through Memories

470
00:29:36,510 --> 00:29:46,510


